WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:21.932
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is ikigai: a reason to rise. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.406
Feel the surface beneath you. Unclench your jaw. Let your shoulders settle. For these five minutes, there is nowhere else you need to be.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:08.170
Notice one breath arriving and one breath leaving. Do not improve it. Let each breath return you to the direct experience of this moment.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:35.981
Ikigai is often described as a grand purpose. It is smaller than that. It is the specific, ordinary reason you got up today, and it may be very small.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.985
It might be someone who would notice your absence. A plant that needs water. Work left half done. Bread you wanted to eat while it was still warm.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.867
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.102
Let one of those come to mind. Do not weigh it or rank it. Notice only where you feel it in the body when you think of it, and breathe there a while.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:23.988
I will leave some quiet here. You do not need to empty the mind. Notice what appears, release the story, and return to breathing.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.427
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:25.684
Give that reason ten minutes before the day fills up. Not the whole of it. Ten minutes, early, while it still belongs to you.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.102
Notice the sounds around you. Invite movement back into your hands and feet. Open your eyes softly. Thank you for meeting this day with Karma.
